Interpretation guide:
  NOTE: the oracle is DOUBLE-OPTIMISTIC (perfect rescue + zero damage).
  A real arbiter (CLIP) also damages GT==winner pixels, so realistic
  gain is a fraction of the ceiling. Decide on these, not the ceiling alone:
    1. per-class oracle Δ : which classes actually have headroom
       (read this, NOT the aggregate rescuable%, since mIoU is per-class).
    2. a pair with HIGH rescue AND LOW breakeven precision
       => CLIP has big upside and an easy precision bar => good target.
    3. if every pair has high breakeven (>~60%) or rescue is tiny
       => CLIP must be near-perfect to help => not worth building.
